# Patch-ID: P-TAB-001 (slice S4) — native content host + attachment lease
# Area: tab.
# Rationale: IPC-CONTRACT §6's view.attach / view.detach / view.resize /
#   view.invalidate verbs need an engine-side native surface and a lease
#   enforcing its rules. S4 ships both, wiring the S1
#   ReArcNativeWindowProvider seam (tab/006) so content's GetNativeWindow()
#   consults resolve to the host's window once a tab is attached.
# Additive only. Files:
#   - content_host_mac.{h,mm} — ReArcContentHostView, a deliberately
#     layerless plain NSView (compositing stays on content's side) owning
#     exactly one content view: the tab's WebContentsView container,
#     anchored via WebContents::GetNativeView() (R8's stable anchor, never
#     GetContentNativeView()/RWHVMac). The header is pure C++: an opaque
#     ReArcContentHostRef (void*) handle plus gfx::NativeView/NativeWindow
#     values (C++ classes usable outside ObjC TUs); every AppKit touch is in
#     the .mm. Create retains via CFBridgingRetain; Release drops ONLY the
#     engine's retain (§6: the shell may retain the emptied NSView until it
#     dismantles its scaffolding). DIP→points rounding with scale-as-hint.
#   - attachment_lease.{h,cc} — AttachmentLeaseRegistry singleton
#     (NoDestructor friend pattern, same as tab/007). §6 rules enforced:
#     at most one live attachment per tab (second attach fails
#     kAlreadyAttached; a lease never grants a second superview);
#     attachments start hidden and WasShown/WasHidden fire only on
#     visibility transitions; engine-allocated monotonic attachment_id
#     from 1 (§1); shell-initiated DetachView empties the host on the main
#     thread and invalidates the id with NO event; engine-initiated
#     InvalidateLeasesForTab empties the host FIRST, releases the engine's
#     retain, then reports view.invalidated to the AttachmentEventSink with
#     the wire-literal reason names ("tab_closed", "window_closed",
#     "content_replaced", "engine_stopped"); expired ids fail (stale
#     attachment) with a VLOG. LeaseWindowProvider backs tab/006's
#     GetNativeWindow() consult with the host's window.
# No call sites are wired in this slice: AttachView/DetachView/ResizeView/
# SetViewVisible are the transport slice's verb handlers;
# InvalidateLeasesForTab(kTabClosed/kContentReplaced/kEngineStopped) is
# invoked by S6's close pipeline, S7's discard, and engine teardown —
# those call sites live in frozen files and arrive via later seams.
# Hunk placement: the BUILD.gn sources block sits after
# "shutdown_watchdog_mac.h" at the end of the is_mac sources list — a -U3
# window fully disjoint from app/005's block (three unchanged lines:
# shell_integration_mac.mm, shutdown_watchdog_mac.cc/.h).
# Gate: build-p9 green on attempt 3 (attempt 1: Cocoa import typo; attempt
# 2: ObjC class declared inside a C++ namespace — declarations must be at
# global scope). nm: full AttachmentLeaseRegistry API + all nine
# ReArcContentHost* entry points present in libchrome_dll.dylib as
# non-external symbols. strings: all four invalidation-reason literals
# present exactly once. --version: 156.0.8078.74.
# Smoke (engine/docs/SMOKE-TEST.md): G1 PASS, G2 PASS, G4 PASS, G5 PASS.
# G3 unchanged: the documented command still trips the BSD grep -q defect
# reported with tab/008 (build-independent); gate intent green (valid PNG
# produced; LC_ALL=C grep -qa PNG PASS).
